# Architecture & Boundaries

pnpm + Turbo monorepo. Workspaces:

- `apps/desktop` - Electron main process (hardware, DB, IPC).
- `apps/renderer` - React frontend (UI only).
- `packages/shared` - types, constants, utilities shared by both.
- `packages/database` - Drizzle schema, migrations, repository functions.

## Strict separation of concerns

- Hardware logic (serial) and database access live ONLY in the Electron main process.
- The renderer NEVER imports `serialport`, `better-sqlite3`, `sql.js`, or any native module.
- All renderer to main communication goes through IPC via the `contextBridge` preload.

```ts
// BAD - in apps/renderer
import { SerialPort } from 'serialport';

// GOOD - in apps/renderer
const ports = await window.electronAPI.listSerialPorts();
```

## Environment & configuration

- Dev: `DB_PATH` env var points to `packages/database/data/dev.db`.
- Prod: the database file lives under `app.getPath('userData')`.
- Migrations run automatically on app startup in production.
